; rungs/novice-1skeleton.eval — ONE encounter, self-contained and repeatable.
;
; A rung is written to be run MANY TIMES with different seeds (`sweep`), so it
; must leave the world exactly as it found it and assume nothing about what ran
; before. Hence: heal, fresh arena, fresh spawn, tally reset — in that order.
;
; It does NOT set the seed. The sweep owns that; a rung that seeded itself would
; produce the same fight every sample and quietly turn a distribution into one
; number repeated N times.

; NOTE: include paths are always relative to the ROOT script's folder, not
; to this file's. The queue is spliced flat, so by the time a line runs there
; is no "including file" left to be relative to. `../presets/...` looked right
; from here and resolved outside the script tree; the runner reported it as an
; unknown line twelve times rather than failing silently.

heal
include presets/novice.eval
arena open 9 9
spawn skeleton 14 9 south
tp 14 12
autoattack on
tally reset
step 45
tally
